IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `fca-definitions`
IMPORT `fca-s3-application`

-- Tests for section 3 of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959.  Every expected value is written beside its assertion, from the text of the Act,
-- before the run.  A failing assertion is a finding, never an edit of the expected value.
--
-- Contract facts, positionally.  The ruler (the fields of `Contract facts`, in order):
--   frustrated, discharged, discharge date, made, Government, charterparty, time charterparty, demise charterparty,
--   carriage of goods by sea, insurance, SGA s 7 applies, specific goods, goods perished

§ `Fixtures -- contracts`

-- An ordinary frustrated contract, made 1 January 2000, discharged 1 June 2020.
`an ordinary frustrated contract` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Discharged on each side of 1 January 1959 (s 3(1)); made on each side of 13 February 1959.
`a contract discharged on 31 December 1958` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 31 12 1958), Date 1 1 1950, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract discharged on 1 January 1959` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 1 1959), Date 1 1 1950, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made before 13 February 1959 and discharged in 1960` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 1960), Date 12 2 1959, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made after 13 February 1959 and discharged in 1960` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 1960), Date 14 2 1959, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract discharged on a date not given` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, NOTHING, Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- A contract to which the Government is a party.
`a contract with the Government` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract with the Government discharged before 1959` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 1958), Date 1 1 1950, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- s 3(5)(a): charterparties and carriage of goods by sea.
`a voyage charterparty` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a time charterparty` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a charterparty by way of demise` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a time charterparty for the carriage of goods by sea` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a bill of lading contract for the carriage of goods by sea` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- s 3(5)(b): insurance.
`a contract of insurance` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- s 3(5)(c): sale of specific goods.
`a contract to which section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sale of specific goods frustrated because the goods perished` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a sale of specific goods frustrated by an export ban` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- s 2(1) conditions that bear on whether the Act applies: not frustrated, not discharged.
`a contract that is not frustrated` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 3(1) by the time of discharge`

-- text: "as respects which the time of discharge is on or after 1 January 1959" -> applies; "but not to contracts as respects which the time of discharge is before that date" -> does not.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract discharged on 31 December 1958` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract discharged on 1 January 1959` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- text: "whether made before or after 13 February 1959": the date of making never changes the result.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract made before 13 February 1959 and discharged in 1960` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract made after 13 February 1959 and discharged in 1960` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to a contract whether made before or after 13 February 1959` (Date 12 2 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to a contract whether made before or after 13 February 1959` (Date 13 2 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to a contract whether made before or after 13 February 1959` (Date 14 2 1959) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to a contract whether made before or after 13 February 1959` (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: no date of the time of discharge is given, so s 3(1) cannot be applied.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract discharged on a date not given` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) this Act applies to the contract by its time of discharge` `a contract that is not frustrated` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3(2) the Government`

-- text: "This Act shall apply to contracts to which the Government is a party in like manner as to contracts between private persons."
#ASSERT `s 3(2) this Act applies in like manner to a contract to which the Government is a party` `a contract with the Government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: a contract with no Government party is outside the sentence.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) this Act applies in like manner to a contract to which the Government is a party` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "in like manner": the Government's contract is subject to the same date rule (before 1959: not applied) and the same answer on a modern date (applied).
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract with the Government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract with the Government discharged before 1959` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Interpretation Act s 2(1): "Government" means the Government of Singapore (copied module, looked up, not re-encoded).
#ASSERT `what the Act names in defining` "Government" EQUALS LIST "Government of Singapore"

§ `Tests -- s 3(5)(a) charterparties and the carriage of goods by sea`

-- text: "(a) to any charterparty, except a time charterparty or a charterparty by way of demise, or to any contract (other than a charterparty) for the carriage of goods by sea"
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a voyage charterparty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a bill of lading contract for the carriage of goods by sea` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the exceptions: NOTHING (the prohibition is limited by its own wording; the paragraph does not say the Act applies to them)
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a time charterparty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a charterparty by way of demise` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(other than a charterparty)": a time charterparty for the carriage of goods by sea is a charterparty, so the second limb does not reach it, and the first limb excepts it.
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a time charterparty for the carriage of goods by sea` EQUALS NOTHING
-- outside the paragraph
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(a) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the whole of s 3: the Act does not apply to a voyage charterparty, and does apply to a time charterparty or a charterparty by way of demise
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a voyage charterparty` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a bill of lading contract for the carriage of goods by sea` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a time charterparty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a charterparty by way of demise` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 3(5)(b) contracts of insurance`

-- text: "(b) to any contract of insurance, except as is provided by section 2(6)"
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(b) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a contract of insurance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(b) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the exception: what section 2(6) provides is not displaced for a contract of insurance (judgment call QA: taken as JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(b) section 2(6) still applies although the contract is a contract of insurance` `a contract of insurance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(b) section 2(6) still applies although the contract is a contract of insurance` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract of insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 3(5)(c) the sale of specific goods`

-- text: "(c) to any contract to which section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 ... applies, or to any other contract for the sale, or for the sale and delivery, of specific goods, where the contract is frustrated by reason of the fact that the goods have perished"
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(c) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a contract to which section 7 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(c) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a sale of specific goods frustrated because the goods perished` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the "where" is not met (the goods have not perished): JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(c) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `a sale of specific goods frustrated by an export ban` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract that is not for the sale of specific goods is outside the paragraph
#ASSERT `s 3(5)(c) this Act shall not apply to the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a sale of specific goods frustrated because the goods perished` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a sale of specific goods frustrated by an export ban` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 3 as a whole`

#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3(1): before 1 January 1959 the Act does not apply, whatever the kind of contract
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract discharged on 31 December 1958` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract discharged on 1 January 1959` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: the time of discharge is not given
#ASSERT `s 3 this Act applies to the contract` `a contract discharged on a date not given` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Fixtures -- provisions and severable parts`

-- Contract provision facts, positionally: a provision for the event of frustration; a provision that has effect whether frustration arises or not.
`a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` MEANS
    `Contract provision facts` OF TRUE, FALSE
`a contract with a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises` MEANS
    `Contract provision facts` OF FALSE, TRUE
`a contract with no such provision` MEANS
    `Contract provision facts` OF FALSE, FALSE

-- Severable part facts, positionally: it appears to the court the part can properly be severed; wholly performed; performed but for the payment of ascertained sums.
`a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a part performed but for the payment of ascertained sums that the court finds severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a part not performed that the court finds severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a wholly performed part that the court finds not severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a wholly performed part where the court has not yet said` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 3(3) the contract's own provision`

-- text: "Where any contract to which this Act applies contains any provision which ... is intended to have effect in the event of circumstances arising which ... frustrate the contract, or is intended to have effect whether such circumstances arise or not, the court shall give effect to that provision"
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision that has effect whether or not frustration arises` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the "where" is not met: no such provision -> JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with no such provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "where" is not met: not a contract to which the Act applies (insurance; discharged before 1959) -> JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `a contract of insurance` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `a contract discharged on 31 December 1958` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: whether the Act applies cannot be told (no date)
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `a contract discharged on a date not given` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "shall only give effect to section 2 to such extent, if any, as appears to the court to be consistent with that provision": never more than section 2 would give, and 0 is possible ("if any")
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` 100 (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` 100 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
-- not covered: the court has not said what is consistent; and the limit does not arise where the contract has no such provision
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the amount of section 2 that is given effect` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with no such provision` 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3(4) severance`

-- text: "Where it appears to the court that a part of any contract to which this Act applies can properly be severed ..., being a part wholly performed before the time of discharge, or so performed except for the payment ... of sums which are or can be ascertained under the contract, the court shall treat that part ... as if it were a separate contract and had not been frustrated"
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part performed but for the payment of ascertained sums that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "where" that is not met: the part is not performed in either way; the court does not find it severable; the Act does not apply
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part not performed that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a wholly performed part that the court finds not severable` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `a contract of insurance` `a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: the court has not said whether it appears the part can be severed; whether the Act applies cannot be told
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a wholly performed part where the court has not yet said` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `a contract discharged on a date not given` `a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` EQUALS NOTHING
-- text: "shall treat section 2 as only applicable to the remainder of that contract": section 2 does not apply to the severed part and does apply to the remainder
#ASSERT `s 3(4) section 2 applies to this portion of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` `the severed part` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) section 2 applies to this portion of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part wholly performed that the court finds severable` `the remainder of the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: where the severance rule does not apply s 3(4) is silent on either portion
#ASSERT `s 3(4) section 2 applies to this portion of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part not performed that the court finds severable` `the severed part` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(4) section 2 applies to this portion of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part not performed that the court finds severable` `the remainder of the contract` EQUALS NOTHING

-- assertions written: 64; satisfied: 64 (check.sh prints the count)
